// Let the console configure its own network.
//
// WHAT BREAKS WITHOUT THIS: nothing, today. That is the problem.
//
// Saving a Wi-Fi connection that comes back after a reboot is the polkit action
// `org.freedesktop.NetworkManager.settings.modify.system`, and its shipped
// default is `auth_admin_keep` — a password prompt. A console has no way to
// answer one: there is no desktop, no polkit agent and nobody at a keyboard
// after first run. So the action has to be granted outright or Wi-Fi cannot be
// set up at all.
//
// It IS granted today, by a rule Bazzite ships for a different reason:
//
//     org.freedesktop.NetworkManager.rules — "Allow users in the wheel group
//     to create system-wide connections ... to maintain backwards
//     compatibility ... This is discouraged otherwise."
//
// The CabinetOS session user is in `wheel` (the image's sysusers.d adds it),
// so Wi-Fi also works by inheritance. `wheel` is also what grants sudo; the
// day the session user leaves it, Wi-Fi configuration would stop working with
// no error anybody would connect to the cause: it presents as a network bug on
// a machine whose network is fine.
//
// So the grant is written down here, naming the one action and the one user,
// and it decouples "may configure the network" from "may become root". Those
// are not the same privilege and should never have been the same grant.
//
// WHY 60-: polkit reads rules.d in lexicographic order and takes the first rule
// that returns a result. Digits sort before letters, so this is consulted
// before Bazzite's `org.freedesktop.NetworkManager.rules` and answers whether
// or not that file is present or still grants anything.
//
// The user name is the one `system_files/usr/lib/sysusers.d/cabinetos.conf`
// creates. If that ever changes, this changes with it — and the check for that
// is `frontend/src/net.cpp`'s `--network` probe, which reports the action's
// polkit result rather than assuming it.
//
// `subject.local` is kept, and it is not ceremony: it means the grant belongs
// to somebody sitting at the machine, not to an SSH session. Developer mode
// hands out SSH deliberately (open question 9), and a shell reached over the
// network should not silently inherit the console's own privileges.

polkit.addRule(function(action, subject) {
    if (action.id == "org.freedesktop.NetworkManager.settings.modify.system" &&
        subject.user == "cabinet" &&
        subject.local) {
        return polkit.Result.YES;
    }
});
